# The connection control's "Stats..." link and the Link Stats window it opens, ported from
# Controls/ConnectionControl.cs, Controls/ConnectionStats.cs and MainV2.cs (ShowConnectionStatsForm,
# ResetConnectionStats, doDisconnect).
#
# The claims: "Stats..." sits under the port box while connected (ConnectionControl.resx linkLabel1
# at 3, 32; IsConnected, ConnectionControl.cs:37-44); its click shows the "Link Stats" dialog with
# the control's boxes empty (MainV2.cs:1259-1283; ConnectionStats.cs:39-47), the ticks as the
# vehicle's state has them - SITL speaks MAVLink 2 and does not sign (:22-24) - and Reset and the
# ticks at their .resx places. At the first quarter second the totals fill: the packets received,
# the bytes in and out, and the longest time between packets in milliseconds (:62-132); the
# packets lost stays empty, a TCP link losing none (WhenPacketLost never fires). From the third
# second the means: packets a second, bytes a second and the quality, 100% with nothing lost
# (:71-97); from the fifth the bytes sent a second (:112-116). A second click shows the window
# already shown. The ticks are the window's own, set by their clicks (:176-184). Reset starts every
# count again: the means empty again for three seconds (:186-190). Disconnecting hides the link and
# leaves the window open with its boxes as they were, no longer counting (StopUpdates,
# MainV2.cs:1407-1418); its close box closes it.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760. Run from the repository root as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/main-link-stats.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# Not yet run: the budget is a guess, set by hand until a passing run records one.

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 16
# 16: 14.8 s measured headless on lavapipe (2026-10-16), the rule's ceiling plus one.

expect vehicle.count > 0
expect vehicle.connected true
expect linkstats.link shown
expect linkstats.window false
expect main-stats below main-port

# Shown: every box empty, the ticks as the vehicle's state has them.
click main-stats
expect linkstats.window true
expect linkstats.updating true
expect linkstats.chk_mavlink2 true
expect linkstats.chk_signing false
expect linkstats-but_reset right-of linkstats-chk_mavlink2
expect linkstats-chk_signing below linkstats-chk_mavlink2

# The quarter second's totals; nothing lost.
expect linkstats.txt_PacketsRx > 0
expect linkstats.txt_BytesReceived ~ b
expect linkstats.txt_BytesSent ~ b
expect linkstats.txt_MaxPacketInterval > 0
expect linkstats.txt_PacketsLost none

# The three seconds' means, then the five seconds' bytes sent.
expect linkstats.txt_PacketsPerSecond > 0
expect linkstats.txt_BytesPerSecondRx ~ b
expect linkstats.txt_LinkQuality 100%
expect linkstats.txt_BytesPerSecondSent ~ b
expect linkstats.since_ms >= 5000

# "Stats..." again: the window already shown, still counting from when it opened.
click main-stats
expect linkstats.window true
expect linkstats.since_ms >= 5000

# The ticks: the window's own, each click turning it over.
click linkstats-chk_mavlink2
expect linkstats.chk_mavlink2 false
click linkstats-chk_mavlink2
expect linkstats.chk_mavlink2 true
click linkstats-chk_signing
expect linkstats.chk_signing true
click linkstats-chk_signing
expect linkstats.chk_signing false

# Reset: every count from now, the means empty again for three seconds.
click linkstats-but_reset
expect linkstats.resets 1
expect linkstats.since_ms < 3000
expect linkstats.txt_PacketsPerSecond none
expect linkstats.txt_PacketsRx > 0
expect linkstats.txt_PacketsPerSecond > 0

# Disconnected: no "Stats...", the window open and frozen.
click main-connect
expect vehicle.connected false
expect linkstats.link hidden
expect linkstats.window true
expect linkstats.updating false
expect linkstats.txt_PacketsRx > 0

# The close box.
click linkstats-close
expect linkstats.window false
